1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,193
Across Karnataka, crime records sit in
silos.

2
00:00:04,193 --> 00:00:12,580
A repeat offender changes one letter of
his name, crosses a district line, and disappears.

3
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,070
The data exists.

4
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:16,400
The intelligence doesn't.

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,125
KSP DAPPA changes that.

6
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:29,300
Built on Zoho Catalyst, it turns
forty-five thousand FIR records — modelled on the official Karnataka Police schema — into one live intelligence hub.

7
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:38,199
A Python pipeline precomputes everything
heavy — hotspots, forecasts, anomaly alerts, the co-accused network.

8
00:00:38,199 --> 00:00:39,832
Data Store holds it.

9
00:00:39,832 --> 00:00:43,016
One Node API serves it in milliseconds.

10
00:00:43,016 --> 00:00:46,200
Caste and religion never enter a model.

11
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:50,056
Live KPI tiles; anomaly districts pulse
red.

12
00:00:50,056 --> 00:00:56,191
Where a table isn't fully loaded, we show
a dash — not a wrong number.

13
00:00:56,191 --> 00:01:01,800
The sixth tile forecasts next month, with
a confidence interval.

14
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,632
GeoIntel ranks every hotspot in the state.

15
00:01:05,632 --> 00:01:08,461
Click one, the map flies to it.

16
00:01:08,461 --> 00:01:14,300
Press space, and months of crime drift
animate across Karnataka.

17
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:24,105
The network explorer maps who offends
together — nearly twenty-four thousand co-accused links across two thousand people.

18
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:28,400
Open a person: the aliases no spreadsheet
could join.

19
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:31,070
Ask DAPPA speaks plain language.

20
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:34,991
Top five districts for vehicle theft this
year?

21
00:01:34,991 --> 00:01:40,748
A chart answers in under a second — and
shows the exact query it ran.

22
00:01:40,748 --> 00:01:43,167
Every AI answer is auditable.

23
00:01:43,167 --> 00:01:52,418
Predict scores case status from a live
QuickML model — and publishes its real accuracy beside it, even when that number is weak.

24
00:01:52,418 --> 00:01:56,538
Zia reads the FIR narrative and pulls out
entities, live.

25
00:01:56,538 --> 00:02:00,730
And the interface switches to Kannada or
Hindi, instantly.

26
00:02:00,730 --> 00:02:05,500
ಇದು ಕರ್ನಾಟಕಕ್ಕಾಗಿ (this is for Karnataka)
— this is for Karnataka.

27
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,425
One Zoho Catalyst project, end to end.

28
00:02:08,425 --> 00:02:14,199
Web Client Hosting serves the app; an
Advanced I/O function serves the API.

29
00:02:14,199 --> 00:02:19,742
Data Store holds forty-five thousand
records; Stratus holds every brief.

30
00:02:19,742 --> 00:02:25,900
QuickML and Zia answer the AI calls —
every response names the engine behind it.

31
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:27,240
Just the start.

32
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:38,322
Today, synthetic FIRs; tomorrow, CCTNS —
same schema, column for column, with jurisdiction-scoped access and an audit trail.

33
00:02:38,322 --> 00:02:41,897
Circuits orchestrates the nightly chain.

34
00:02:41,897 --> 00:02:44,667
Ask DAPPA out loud, in Kannada.

35
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:45,867
KSP DAPPA.

36
00:02:45,867 --> 00:02:48,223
From records to foresight.

37
00:02:48,223 --> 00:02:54,634
Built end to end on Zoho Catalyst, for the
KSP Datathon twenty twenty-six.

